	(text_box "When at the local thrift store I just had to spend the $5\non a calculator that had the style I loved. It was clean\nand in good shape and mostly worked but the screen suffered\nfrom a couple dead lines in the dot matrix and I realized \nhow slow those devices were. So I decided it would be a fun\nproject to get a new display put in it. Then, scope creep.\n\nNow we're puting the finishing touches on a WiFi/BT Linux\npowered color LCD with USB-C charging LiPo battery. \nSomeday I may even get around to making it compute the sum \nof two integers."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 27.94 0)
		(size 101.6 38.1)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
